[5.601963, "o", "{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01PbUKRUVwuUnzji5v3mVi7q\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1\\t# Test Coverage Gap Report\\n2\\t\\n3\\t**Library:** PathFinding.js  \\n4\\t**Audited:** 2026-04-16  \\n5\\t**Test run:** 294 passing, 0 failing (2s)\\n6\\t\\n7\\t---\\n8\\t\\n9\\t## Summary\\n10\\t\\n11\\tCoverage is strong on happy paths and constructor options. Gaps concentrate in:\\n12\\t- **edge-case branches** inside `_jump` / `_findNeighbors` for JPS variants\\n13\\t- **BiAStar / BiBFS** meeting-from-end branch + start==end\\n14\\t- **Util** `smoothenPath` bug surface and `expandPath` contract for short paths\\n15\\t- **Grid** out-of-bounds mutation and `IfAtMostOneObstacle` diagonal corner cases\\n16\\t\\n17\\t---\\n18\\t\\n19\\t## `src/core/Util.js`\\n20\\t\\n21\\t### What IS tested\\n22\\t- `interpolate` — vertical, horizontal, diagonal, same-point\\n23\\t- `expandPath` — empty array, 2-segment path\\n24\\t- `compressPath` — empty, single, two-element, multi-segment\\n25\\t- `backtrace` — chain, single node"]
[5.602276, "o", "\\n26\\t- `biBacktrace` — two chains merge\\n27\\t- `pathLength` — single node, horizontal, diagonal, multi-step\\n28\\t- `smoothenPath` — clear grid (no waypoints), single obstacle triggers waypoint\\n29\\t\\n30\\t### What is NOT tested\\n31\\t\\n32\\t| Function | Missing case | Priority |\\n33\\t|---|---|---|\\n34\\t| `smoothenPath` | Path length < 2 — `len < 2` skips `for` loop, returns `[[x0,y0], [x1,y1]]` where both points come from `path[0]` and `path[len-1]`; for a 1-node path these are identical → silent wrong output | **high** |\\n35\\t| `smoothenPath` | Multiple obstacles in sequence — `lastValidCoord` implicit-global bug at line 167 (`lastValidCoord` never declared with `var`) gets shared across calls in strict mode environments; no test with two separate obstacle segments | **high** |\\n36\\t| `smoothenPath` | Two-node path (len==2) — loop body never runs; result should be `[start, end]` | **medium** |\\n37\\t| `expandPath` | Single-element path — `len < 2` returns `[]` not `[path[0]]`; this silent empty-"]
[5.602327, "o", "return is undocumented | **medium** |\\n38\\t| `interpolate` | Both axes negative direction (`x1 < x0 && y1 < y0`) — `sx=-1, sy=-1` branch untested directly | **low** |\\n39\\t| `compressPath` | 3-element collinear straight path → should compress to 2 elements | **low** |\\n40\\t\\n41\\t---\\n42\\t\\n43\\t## `src/core/Grid.js`\\n44\\t\\n45\\t### What IS tested\\n46\\t- Constructor: width+height, matrix, matrix-only (auto dimensions)\\n47\\t- `_buildNodes`: matrix size mismatch throws\\n48\\t- `isWalkableAt`, `isInside`, `setWalkableAt`\\n49\\t- `getNeighbors`: Never, IfAtMostOneObstacle (partial), Always (partial), OnlyWhenNoObstacles (partial), invalid value throws\\n50\\t- `clone`: walkability mirrored, mutation isolation\\n51\\t- Corner nodes: no out-of-bounds neighbors with Always\\n52\\t\\n53\\t### What is NOT tested\\n54\\t\\n55\\t| Method | Missing case | Priority |\\n56\\t|---|---|---|\\n57\\t| `getNeighbors` — `IfAtMostOneObstacle` | Each diagonal flag individually: d0=s3\\\\|\\\\|s0, d1=s0\\\\|\\\\|s1, d2=s1\\\\|\\\\|s2, d3=s2\\\\|\\\\|s3. Key dist"]
