[27.049151, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-6\",\"id\":\"msg_015dSVdXgRN5TaWNM2Xom2LB\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now I need to distribute work. Let me analyze the gaps:\\n\\n**Coverage gaps by area:**\\n\\n1. **Util.js** - smoothenPath (3 cases, 2 high), expandPath (1 medium), interpolate (1 low), compressPath (1 low) — medium effort\\n2. **Grid.js** - getNeighbors IfAtMostOneObstacle (1 high), OnlyWhenNoObstacles (1 medium), setWalkableAt/getNodeAt OOB (2 medium), clone (1 low), _buildNodes (1 low) — medium effort\\n\\n\\n3. **Node.js** - just 2 low priority cases to handle\\n4. **Bi-directional finders** (BiAStar, BiBFS, BiDijkstra, BiBestFirst) - this is the biggest chunk with start==end scenarios (4 high), meeting-from-end logic (3 high), constructor heuristic wrapping (1 high), and various updateItem/no-path cases (several medium) — large effort\\n5. **AStar/Dijkstra/BFS/BestFirst** (non-bi) - scattered medium and low priority cases — small-medium e"]
[27.049636, "o", "ffort\\n6. **IDAStarFinder** - start==end (high), deprecated flags (medium), trackRecursion state (medium) — medium effort\\n7. **JumpPointFinder** - appears to be cut off but likely has similar coverage gaps to address\\n8. **JPS variants** - JPFAlwaysMoveDiagonally with jump forced neighbors (3 high, 3 medium), JPFMoveDiagonallyIfAtMostOneObstacle with jump vertical (1 high, 3 medium), JPFMoveDiagonallyIfNoObstacles (4 high, 6 medium), JPFNeverMoveDiagonally (5 high, 3 medium), plus JumpPointFinderBase and factory (3 medium and 1 medium respectively) — this is a massive effort\\n9. **Visual/scenario work** - 12 scenarios identified from the visual audit that need to be built out\\n\\nNow I'm thinking about how to split this work: test-writer-1 should take the core utility modules (Util.js, Grid.js, Node.js) since they're foundational and related, while test-writer-2 tackles the bi-directional finders since they all share similar patterns and logic.\\n\\nActually, I'm realizing JPS has too many gaps to handle cl"]
[27.050344, "o", "eanly. Let me rebalance by splitting JPS across two writers instead. I'll pair the core modules with the simpler non-directional finders (AStar, Dijkstra, BFS, BestFirst) for test-writer-1, then have test-writer-2 handle all the bi-directional variants (BiAStar, BiBFS, BiDijkstra, BiBestFirst).\\n\\nThat leaves test-writer-3 and test-writer-4 to split up the JPS variants more evenly. This distribution feels more balanced—writer 1 has volume but mostly straightforward items, writer 2 gets the high-priority bi-directional stuff, and writers 3 and 4 share the JPS complexity. I'll also need a scenario-builder to handle the visual test cases from the audit. Now I'm ready to start writing the files.\",\"signature\":\""]
