[126.977589, "o", " IDA*, pick Euclidean in IDA* panel, run search. Verify heuristic actually used matches selection, not JPS panel.\\n\\n## Priority 2 — No \\\"path not found\\\" feedback\\n\\n**File:** `visual/js/view.js:245`\\n**Scenario:** Surround start node with walls. Run any algorithm. Verify user gets clear \\\"No path found\\\" message instead of silent finish with `length: 0`.\\n\\n## Priority 3 — Start equals end\\n\\n**Scenario:** Drag end node onto start node position. Run search. Verify no crash, graceful zero-length path or no-op.\\n\\n## Priority 4 — Drag start/end during search\\n\\n**Scenario:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating. Verify state machine blocks drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states). No crash or state corruption.\\n\\n## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\\n\\n**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\\n\\n## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\\n\\n**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation c"]
[126.977638, "o", "ontinues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped operations.\\n\\n## Priority 7 — Restart during search\\n\\n**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\\n\\n## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\\n\\n**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\\n**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\\n\\n## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\\n\\n**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explores fewer nodes; same or similar path.\\n\\n## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\\n\\n**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\\n\\n## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\\n\\n**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms,"]
