[219.019246, "o", "n Grid** — no obstacles, all algorithms. Verify path drawn, node coloring correct, stats display.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\",\"+7. **Blocked Grid (no path)** — solid wall. All algorithms. Verify no path drawn, no crash, finished state clean.\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\",\"+8. **Start==End (degenerate)** — drag end to start position. Verify path length 0/1, no crash, no NaN in stats.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\",\"+9. **Pause and Resume** — A* large grid, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation stops/resumes cleanly.\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation continues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped operations.\",\"+10. **Drag Start/End in Finished State** — run algorithm, drag node. Verify state transition to `modified`, buttons update.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 7 — Restart during search\",\"+### Priority 3 — Algorithm Comp"]
[219.019263, "o", "arison Scenarios\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\",\"+11. **Diagonal Toggle** — A* Manhattan diagonal on vs off. Verify path length difference.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\",\"+12. **Don't Cross Corners** — diagonal passage, `dontCrossCorners` on vs off. Verify corner-cutting behavior.\",\" \",\"-**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\",\"-**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\",\"+13. **Bi-directional Toggle** — A* uni vs bi. Verify ~half node expansion.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\",\"+14. **IDA* Time Limit** — complex maze, 1s limit. Verify search terminates, UI handles gracefully.\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explore"]
[219.019286, "o", "s fewer nodes; same or similar path.\",\"+15. **JPS vs A* Node Expansion** — large open grid. Verify JPS expands far fewer nodes.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\",\"+16. **Weighted A*** — weight=1 vs weight=5. Verify fewer operations with higher weight.\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\",\"+17. **Orthogonal JPS vs BFS** — obstacles, no diagonal. Verify same path length, fewer JPS nodes.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\",\"+### Priority 4 — Missing UI Features (Document Only)\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms, run IDA*. Verify IDA* aborts at time limit with some feedback.\",\"+18. **Missing JPS diagonal modes** — `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` not in UI. Document that `JumpPointFinder` factory supports them but panel has no entry point.\",\" \",\"-## Priority 12 — Full grid walls\",\"+19. **Animation speed not configurable** — hardcoded 300 ops/s"]
[219.019299, "o", "ec at `controller.js:95`.\",\" \",\"-**Scenario:** Draw walls everywhere. Run search. Verify robust no-path handling, no JS errors.\",\"-\",\"-## Priority 13 — Large operation count performance\",\"-\",\"-**Scenario:** Dijkstra or BFS on open 64x36 grid, start top-left, end bottom-right. Verify animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec.\",\"-\",\"-## Priority 14 — Adjacent start/end\",\"-\",\"-**Scenario:** Start and end nodes 1 step apart. Verify minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish.\",\"+20. **Grid size not configurable** — hardcoded 64×36 at `controller.js:94`.\"]}],\"originalFile\":\"# Scenario Builder — Visual & UI Test Scenarios\\n\\n## Scope\\nBuild test scenarios for the visual demo app based on gaps identified in the visual audit.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Priority 1 — Bug: IDA* heuristic reads wrong radio group\\n\\n**File:** `visual/js/panel.js:160`\\n**Bug:** Reads `input[name=jump_point_heuristic]` instead of `input[name=ida_heuristic]`\\n**Scenario:** Select IDA*, pick Euclidean in IDA* panel, run search. Verify heuristic"]
[219.019311, "o", " actually used matches selection, not JPS panel.\\n\\n## Priority 2 — No \\\"path not found\\\" feedback\\n\\n**File:** `visual/js/view.js:245`\\n**Scenario:** Surround start node with walls. Run any algorithm. Verify user gets clear \\\"No path found\\\" message instead of silent finish with `length: 0`.\\n\\n## Priority 3 — Start equals end\\n\\n**Scenario:** Drag end node onto start node position. Run search. Verify no crash, graceful zero-length path or no-op.\\n\\n## Priority 4 — Drag start/end during search\\n\\n**Scenario:** Begin search, attempt to drag start/end while animating. Verify state machine blocks drag (only allowed in `ready`/`finished` states). No crash or state corruption.\\n\\n## Priority 5 — Wall on start or end position\\n\\n**Scenario:** Place wall on start node position. Run search. Expect graceful failure, not crash.\\n\\n## Priority 6 — Pause / Resume cycle\\n\\n**Scenario:** Start search, pause mid-animation, resume. Verify animation continues from exact paused state with no duplicate or skipped ope"]
[219.019324, "o", "rations.\\n\\n## Priority 7 — Restart during search\\n\\n**Scenario:** Start search, click Restart before finish. Verify animation clears, new search begins cleanly, no stale colored nodes remain.\\n\\n## Priority 8 — JPS diagonal modes not selectable\\n\\n**Gap:** Only 2 of 4 JumpPointFinder diagonal modes exposed in UI. `Always` and `OnlyWhenNoObstacles` missing.\\n**Scenario:** Document what UI changes needed; build scenario that exercises all 4 modes if dropdown were added.\\n\\n## Priority 9 — Bi-directional vs unidirectional comparison\\n\\n**Scenario:** Same grid, run A* unidirectional then bi-directional. Verify bi-directional explores fewer nodes; same or similar path.\\n\\n## Priority 10 — Weight parameter effect\\n\\n**Scenario:** Run A* with weight=1 vs weight=5 on same grid. Higher weight → fewer operations (greedier) but potentially longer path.\\n\\n## Priority 11 — IDA* time limit\\n\\n**Scenario:** Dense wall grid, set time limit to 1ms, run IDA*. Verify IDA* aborts at time limit with some feedback.\\n"]
[219.01958, "o", "\\n## Priority 12 — Full grid walls\\n\\n**Scenario:** Draw walls everywhere. Run search. Verify robust no-path handling, no JS errors.\\n\\n## Priority 13 — Large operation count performance\\n\\n**Scenario:** Dijkstra or BFS on open 64x36 grid, start top-left, end bottom-right. Verify animation remains smooth at 300 ops/sec.\\n\\n## Priority 14 — Adjacent start/end\\n\\n**Scenario:** Start and end nodes 1 step apart. Verify minimal animation, path length ~1, fast finish.\\n\",\"userModified\":false}}\r\n"]
